      <p><c>*************************************************</c></p>
      <p><c>So far what we have done:</c></p>
      <p><c>1. written DB connection in db&amp;gt;index.js</c></p>
      <p><c>2. created express server in app.js</c></p>
      <p><c>3. index.js - we have called DB connection function and initiated connection, then() - is connection succesfulll then() part of the function will excute where started the server.</c></p>
      <p><c>Project moving forward.....</c></p>
      <p><c>middlewares</c></p>
      <p><c>what is a middleware?</c></p>
      <p><c>-&amp;gt; middleware is the function which will exceute at server side on req and res.</c></p>
      <p><c>middleware written as below:</c></p>
      <p><c>function middleware(err, req, res, next)</c></p>
      <p><c>The position of midleware in flow is as below:</c></p>
      <p><c>req:</c></p>
      <p><c>client sent data over stream</c></p>
      <p><c>=&amp;gt; raw Stream</c></p>
      <p><c>=&amp;gt; middleware parses</c></p>
      <p><c>=&amp;gt; req.body created</c></p>
      <p><c>=&amp;gt; route handler and server perform action on req.</c></p>
      <p><c>res:</c></p>
      <p><c>route handler calls res methods</c></p>
      <p><c>=&amp;gt; res object created</c></p>
      <p><c>=&amp;gt; middleware (transform or add token to response)</c></p>
      <p><c>=&amp;gt; raw stream sent to client.</c></p>
      <p><c>Working forward on express, main focus in express will be req and res.</c></p>
      <p><c>working worward on request part of the express.</c></p>
      <p><c>installed</c></p>
      <p><c>cors</c></p>
      <p><c>and</c></p>
      <p><c>cookie-parser</c></p>
      <p><c>app.use -</c></p>
      <p><c>it will be used for the middleware</c></p>
      <p><c>cors is a middleware and will be initited using app.</c></p>
      <p><c>//its simple form to mention the cors</c></p>
      <p><c>app.use(cors());</c></p>
      <p><c>//advanced form to mention the cors, env need to set or use direct value here</c></p>
      <p><c>app.use(cors({</c></p>
      <p><c>origin:process.env.CORS_ORIGIN,</c></p>
      <p><c>credentials:true</c></p>
      <p><c>}))</c></p>
      <p><c>**************************************</c></p>
      <p><c>json file limit</c></p>
      <p><c>express.json()</c></p>
      <p><c>express.json() is a middleware that parses the incoming JSON payloads in the request body.</c></p>
      <p><c>can customise the properties as below:</c></p>
      <p><c>1)</c></p>
      <p><c>limit</c></p>
      <p><c>: ”16kb”</c></p>
      <p><c>2)</c></p>
      <p><c>strict</c></p>
      <p><c>: true</c></p>
      <p><c>If its true then accept only json objects and arrays</c></p>
      <p><c>if its false then accept primitive JSON values like number and string.</c></p>
      <p><c>3)</c></p>
      <p><c>reviver</c></p>
      <p><c>- its a function that can transform the parsed json values before putting them in req.body.</c></p>
      <p><c>app.use(express.json({</c></p>
      <p><c>reviver:(key, value)=&amp;gt;{</c></p>
      <p><c>if( typeof value ==="String”) return value.toUpperCase();</c></p>
      <p><c>return value;</c></p>
      <p><c>}}))</c></p>
      <p><c>4)</c></p>
      <p><c>type</c></p>
      <p><c>- determine which requests are parsed.</c></p>
      <p><c>default ‘application/json’</c></p>
      <p><c>If client sends data in form of req like text/html then have to add the middleware here in order to parse the in text/html format</c></p>
      <p><c>5.</c></p>
      <p><c>inflate</c></p>
      <p><c>- it will automatically decompress gzipped or dflated request bodies.</c></p>
      <p><c>default is true</c></p>
      <p><c>limit: '1mb',</c></p>
      <p><c>strict: true,</c></p>
      <p><c>reviver: null,</c></p>
      <p><c>type: 'application/json',</c></p>
      <p><c>inflate: true</c></p>
      <p><c>}));</c></p>
      <p><c>*****************************************</c></p>
      <p><c>app.use(express.urlencoded({extended:true, limit:”16kb”}))</c></p>
      <p><c>This middleware used to parse application/x-www=urlencoded request.</c></p>
      <p><c>example data which will come in url</c></p>
      <p><c>username=ravi&amp;amp;age=28</c></p>
      <p><c>after parsing, express puut it in req.body</c></p>
      <p><c>req.body = {username:"ravi”, age:”28”}</c></p>
      <p><c>**********************</c></p>
      <p><c>app.use(express.static(“public”))</c></p>
      <p><c>-----------------------------------------------------------------------</c></p>
