      <p><c>Create a model in mongoose.</c></p>
      <p><c>user.model.js</c></p>
      <p><c>video.model.js</c></p>
      <p><c>--------------------------------------------------------------------</c></p>
      <p><c>mongoose-aggregate-paginate-v2</c></p>
      <p><c>Need to install above package</c></p>
      <p><c>.</c></p>
      <p><c>Use Case</c></p>
      <p><c>-</c></p>
      <p><c>Suppose you have 1000 users in your MongoDB collection.</c></p>
      <p><c>Without pagination:</c></p>
      <p><c>GET /users</c></p>
      <p><c>[</c></p>
      <p><c>{ "id": 1, "name": "Ravi" },</c></p>
      <p><c>{ "id": 2, "name": "John" },</c></p>
      <p><c>...</c></p>
      <p><c>{ "id": 1000, "name": "Alex" }</c></p>
      <p><c>]</c></p>
      <p><c>This would send all</c></p>
      <p><c>1000</c></p>
      <p><c>records at once (slow + heavy for client)</c></p>
      <p><c>with pagination</c></p>
      <p><c>limit =</c></p>
      <p><c>10</c></p>
      <p><c>per page</c></p>
      <p><c>GET/users?page=1&amp;amp;limit=10</c></p>
      <p><c>response from database would be as below</c></p>
      <p><c>"docs": [</c></p>
      <p><c>{ "id": 10, "name": "Alex" }</c></p>
      <p><c>],</c></p>
      <p><c>"page": 1,</c></p>
      <p><c>"totalPages": 100</c></p>
      <p><c>Client get 10 users at a time and if required client can request for more.</c></p>
      <p><c>Perfomance</c></p>
      <p><c>: Pagination improve prformance and dont overload server or client with huge data dump.</c></p>
      <p><c>Faster Loading</c></p>
      <p><c>: Only some part of data being fetched</c></p>
      <p><c>Better UX</c></p>
      <p><c>: User scrolls or click “ next page” instead of waiting for evrything.</c></p>
      <p><c>Pagination = breaking result into pages, this package helps us to do that for mongoDB aggtregative queries.</c></p>
      <p><c>How to use in model.</c></p>
      <p><c>Suppose we have video model, where we will have multiple videos stored so we will use</c></p>
      <p><c>mongoose-aggregate-paginate-v2 in this model.</c></p>
      <p><c>//code as below</c></p>
      <p><c>import mongoose, { Schema } from "mongoose";</c></p>
      <p><c>import mongooseAggregatePaginate from "mongoose-aggregate-paginate-v2";</c></p>
      <p><c>const videoSchema = new Schema({},{});</c></p>
      <p><c>videoSchema.plugin(mongooseAggregatePaginate);</c></p>
      <p><c>export const Video = mongoose.model(“Video”, videoSchema)</c></p>
      <p><c>***********************************************</c></p>
      <p><c>Some more libraries:</c></p>
      <p><c>node.bcrypt.js - This library help you hash the password.</c></p>
      <p><c>jsonwebtoken - JWT,</c></p>
      <p><c>In order to use above features into the code do below.</c></p>
      <p><c>1. These feature / action will be run before sving data in database and after user perfoam save operation.</c></p>
      <p><c>user clicked on save = &amp;gt; middleware =&amp;gt; database operation performaed and saved date.</c></p>
      <p><c>2. use mongoose middleware.</c></p>
      <p><c>use Pre hook of mongoosse middleware to perform actions, like encrypt password</c></p>
      <p><c>https://mongoosejs.com/docs/middleware.html#pre</c></p>
      <p><c>3.</c></p>
      <p><c>bcrypt</c></p>
      <p><c>userSchema.pre("save", async function (next) {</c></p>
      <p><c>//</c></p>
      <p><c>check if password field modified, return if not password modified</c></p>
      <p><c>if (!this.isModified("password")) return next();</c></p>
      <p><c>this.password = bcrypt.hash(this.password, 10);</c></p>
      <p><c>});</c></p>
      <p><c>create a custom method to check if password is correct</c></p>
      <p><c>userSchema.methods.isPasswordCorrect = async function(password){</c></p>
      <p><c>return await bcrypt.compare(password, this.password);</c></p>
      <p><c>4. JWT - JWT is bearer token.</c></p>
      <p><c>JWT (JSON Web Token) is a compact, URL-safe token format used for securely transmitting information between client and server.</c></p>
      <p><c>A JWT has three parts, separated by dots (.)</c></p>
      <p><c>Header.Payload.Signature</c></p>
      <p><c>Create secret tokens in .env file</c></p>
      <p><c>ACCESS_TOKEN_SECRET=4a20780449da3e09f0f0ffdae1dc909cc884d96c08553a14402a8c066441f0bb</c></p>
      <p><c>ACCESS_TOKEN_EXPIRY=1d</c></p>
      <p><c>REFRESH_TOKEN_SECRET=66b148fec838e56c717745baf0d0bde5c302c3d0836e6e7fcd9a5554cc62307e</c></p>
      <p><c>REFRESH_TOKEN_EXPIRY=10d</c></p>
      <p><c>create a refresh token and access token into User model:</c></p>
      <p><c>userSchema.methods.generateAccessToken = function(){</c></p>
      <p><c>return jwt.sign(</c></p>
      <p><c>_id : this.id,</c></p>
      <p><c>email : this.email,</c></p>
      <p><c>username : this.username,</c></p>
      <p><c>fullName : this.fullName,</c></p>
      <p><c>},</c></p>
      <p><c>process.env.ACCESS_TOKEN_SECRET,</c></p>
      <p><c>expiresIn:process.env.ACCESS_TOKEN_EXPIRY</c></p>
      <p><c>)</c></p>
      <p><c>How to upload file in backend</c></p>
