      <p><c>Controllers</c></p>
      <p><c>Create a folder like this:</c></p>
      <p><c>folder - Controller - user.controller.js</c></p>
      <p><c>We write the controller like as below</c></p>
      <p><c>const useController = (req, res) =&amp;gt;{</c></p>
      <p><c>res.status(200).json({message:"OK”});</c></p>
      <p><c>The most effective way fo wriiting this controller flow is as below:</c></p>
      <p><c>Step 1: Create a syncHandler</c></p>
      <p><c>Folder - util- asyncHandler.js</c></p>
      <p><c>const asyncHandler= (handlerFunction) =&amp;gt;{</c></p>
      <p><c>return (res, res, next) =&amp;gt;{Promise.resolve(handlerFunction(req, res)).catch((err)=&amp;gt; next(err))}</c></p>
      <p><c>export {asyncHandler}</c></p>
      <p><c>// from above asyncHandler if there is any error then it will be passed to the centralized error handler middleware</c></p>
      <p><c>Step 2: Create centralized error hander midleware</c></p>
      <p><c>Folder - middlewares - errohandler.middleware.js</c></p>
      <p><c>const errorHandler = (err, req,res, next) =&amp;gt;{</c></p>
      <p><c>const statusCode = err.status || 500;</c></p>
      <p><c>res.status(statusCode).json({message: err.message || “Internal Error”, stack:err.stack})</c></p>
      <p><c>export {errorHandler}</c></p>
      <p><c>Step 3: Create controller by inserting</c></p>
      <p><c>asynchHandler</c></p>
      <p><c>Folder - controllers - user.controller.js</c></p>
      <p><c>const userController = asyncHandler(req, res, next)=&amp;gt;{</c></p>
      <p><c>export {userController}</c></p>
      <p><c>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</c></p>
      <p><c>Logic Building</c></p>
      <p><c>The steps in logic involed:</c></p>
      <p><c>1. Get the user details from frontend</c></p>
      <p><c>2. Validation - Check if not empty etc etc</c></p>
      <p><c>3. Check if that room category already exist</c></p>
      <p><c>4. check for images if uplaoded on server or not</c></p>
      <p><c>5. upload images to cloudinary and check if uploaded succesfully on cloudinary or not</c></p>
      <p><c>6. Create a room category object - create entry in db</c></p>
      <p><c>7. Remove password and refresh token feild from response.</c></p>
      <p><c>8. Check for room category creation</c></p>
      <p><c>9. return res</c></p>
      <p><c>Create a controller which will read the req.body and process thet information.</c></p>
      <p><c>examples:</c></p>
      <p><c>const addUser = asyncHandler((req,res, next)=&amp;gt;{</c></p>
      <p><c>const {name. email, password } = req.body;</c></p>
      <p><c>export default addUser;</c></p>
      <p><c>In above example this controller will be passed to router , where router will invoke the</c></p>
      <p><c>post</c></p>
      <p><c>request.</c></p>
      <p><c>Router logic:</c></p>
      <p><c>import addUser from ‘../controllers/addUser.controller.js";</c></p>
      <p><c>import express from “express”;</c></p>
      <p><c>const router = express.Router();</c></p>
      <p><c>router.post(“/user”, addUser)</c></p>
      <p><c>export default router;</c></p>
      <p><c>S</c></p>
      <p><c>er</c></p>
      <p><c>ve</c></p>
      <p><c>r.js</c></p>
      <p><c>import userRouter from “./Router/userRouter.js”;</c></p>
      <p><c>//Need middleware to process the json data</c></p>
      <p><c>app.use(express.json());</c></p>
      <p><c>app.use(“/api”,</c></p>
      <p><c>userRouter</c></p>
      <p><c>);</c></p>
      <p><c>Validation will be done in controller. Like as below</c></p>
      <p><c>import {ApiError} from ‘./util/ApiError.js’;</c></p>
      <p><c>const addUser = asyncHandler((req, res, next)=&amp;gt;{</c></p>
      <p><c>const {name, email, password} = req.body;</c></p>
      <p><c>if([name,email, password].some((field)=&amp;gt; field.trim()==="”))</c></p>
      <p><c>throw new ApiError(400,"All fields are required”);</c></p>
      <p><c>In this situiation we will be directly checking with database if any same room category already exit.</c></p>
      <p><c>Here we will communicate with the db with the help of mongoose model.</c></p>
      <p><c>So while admin add the new room category, I will check if that room name or room code already exist</c></p>
      <p><c>I will do like this</c></p>
      <p><c>We have a model created and exported</c></p>
      <p><c>export const RoomCategory = mongoose.model("RoomCategory", roomCategorySchema);</c></p>
      <p><c>We will consider only 4 input data as of now for sample</c></p>
      <p><c>I can create a controller like</c></p>
      <p><c>import { RoomCategory } from ‘../models/roomCategory.model.js”;</c></p>
      <p><c>const roomController = ayncHandler((req, res, next)=&amp;gt;{</c></p>
      <p><c>const {name, code, location, info} = req.body;</c></p>
      <p><c>//validation done to check if its not empty</c></p>
      <p><c>// check if duplicate name or code.</c></p>
      <p><c>const existingCategory = RoomCategory.findOne({</c></p>
      <p><c>$or: [{name}, {code}]</c></p>
      <p><c>if(existingCategory){</c></p>
      <p><c>throw new ApiError(409, “Category or category code already exist”)};</c></p>
      <p><c>I</c></p>
      <p><c>n</c></p>
      <p><c>above example we have directly checked the existing data or duplication with database.</c></p>
      <p><c>4. Use multer middleware to upload the images or files etc.</c></p>
      <p><c>This operation wil be done in the router. Bcoz router has specified the route and the request time.</c></p>
      <p><c>We need to import the mutler middleware where upload was exported.</c></p>
      <p><c>import {upload} from “../middleWares/multerMiddleware.js”</c></p>
      <p><c>router.post(“/user”,</c></p>
      <p><c>upload.fields([{name:"bannerImg”, maxCount:1},{name:"roomImg”, maxCount:3}])</c></p>
      <p><c>,addUser)</c></p>
      <p><c>5. Upload the image to cloudinary</c></p>
      <p><c>)}</c></p>
      <p><c>//upload the images to cloudinary</c></p>
      <p><c>//since we have already created a cloudinary in util -&amp;gt; cloudinary.js and exported {</c></p>
      <p><c>uploadToCloudinary</c></p>
      <p><c>//also we have used mutler middlerware, so it will give files in request. Lets catch it</c></p>
      <p><c>const bannerImgPath = req.files?.bannerImg[0]?.path;</c></p>
      <p><c>const roomImgPath = req,files?.roomImg[0]?.path;</c></p>
      <p><c>const bannerImg = await</c></p>
      <p><c>uploadToCloudinary(bannerImgPath);</c></p>
      <p><c>const roomImg = await uploadToCloudinary(roomImgPath);</c></p>
      <p><c>//validation, if image not provided</c></p>
      <p><c>if(!bannerImg)</c></p>
      <p><c>{thorw new ApiError(400,"banner Img required’)}</c></p>
      <p><c>// Create a object to push all image data to database</c></p>
      <p><c>//here again we will use our model schema</c></p>
      <p><c>RoomCategory.create({</c></p>
      <p><c>name,</c></p>
      <p><c>email,</c></p>
      <p><c>bannerImg:bannerImg.url, // cloudinary returned object which have url</c></p>
      <p><c>roomImg:roomImg?.url || "”,</c></p>
      <p><c>passoword,</c></p>
